      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose.\n\n- **Maximum daily dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US). Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Maximum single dose:** about 1,000 mg for immediate-release, and 850 mg is the usual TID unit.\n- **Risk:** this dose greatly raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nThe intended dose may have been one of these:\n- 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO BID with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO TID with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, for example 850 mg BID\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg TID is truly intended, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale for the order note."
      }
     ],
